    {
      "id": "fh7fb9f",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7.1 Forest Cover"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Chhattisgarh ranks 3rd in India for total forest cover, spanning over 44% of its geographical area.",
        ",The state has three major National Parks: Indravati, Kanger Valley, and Guru Ghasidas (Sanjay) National Park.",
        "There are 11 designated Wildlife Sanctuaries, with Tamor Pingla being the largest and Badalkhol being the smallest.",
        "The State Animal of Chhattisgarh is the Wild Buffalo (Bubalus arnee) and the State Bird is the Hill Myna (Gracula religiosa).",
        "Chitrakote Waterfall on the Indravati River is widely known as the 'Niagara of India'."
      ],
      "id": "yc4p1w2"
    },
