    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c8a9uhv",
      "content": "Chhattisgarh is one of the most forested states of India. About 44% of the state's geographical area is covered by forests, which is among the highest in the country. The forests are primarily concentrated in the Bastar, Surguja, and Jashpur regions."
    },
